Subject: A compiled push that does not fit the array's capacity runs the builtin instead of leaving

What this does
  - `qjs_aot_array_push_slow(ctx, arr, v, out)` (exported to the units, declared in quickjs-aot-rt.h) pushes one value through `js_array_push`, the engine's own builtin, and returns the new length. If the builtin throws (out of memory)
    it clears the exception and returns 0.
  - The inline push of a compiled body (`q2_array_push1`, generated) calls it when the array has no spare capacity or its packed element kind has none, instead of leaving for the generic call.

Why we need it
  `new Array()` starts with capacity 0, so every first push (and every growth step) left the compiled body: in deltablue `OrderedCollection.add` left 56,730 times per unit and each exit repeated the call (about 250 instructions).
  With the helper those pushes stay in compiled code: deltablue 782.0 -> 758.7 C.Minstr.

Soundness
  The helper is called only after the body checked what the inline push checks before it writes (`q2_array_plain`: standard array shape and prototype, extensible, length equals the count and is writable, the callee is the builtin `push`), so no JS runs. It allocates but cannot run
  a collection (js_malloc does not). An out-of-memory exception is cleared and the body leaves before any effect, so the generic body repeats the call and throws it properly. The value pushed is counted by the builtin.

Functions touched
  `qjs_aot_array_push_slow` (new).

No.

--- a/quickjs-aot-rt.h
+++ b/quickjs-aot-rt.h
@@ -227,0 +228,2 @@
+/* push of one value through the builtin on a plain array the body checked (the capacity miss of the inline push); 0 = it threw and nothing happened */
+QJS_AOT_STUB int qjs_aot_array_push_slow(JSContext *ctx, JSValue arr, JSValue v, JSValue *out);
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -65239,0 +65240,16 @@
+}
+
+/* The push of a compiled body that does not fit the array's capacity (or its packed element kind): the builtin itself, on a receiver the
+   body has already checked is a plain extensible array whose length is the count and whose prototype is the standard one, so no JS can
+   run. Returns 1 with the new length in *out; 0 when the push threw (an out-of-memory), after clearing the exception, so the body leaves
+   before any effect and its generic body repeats the call and throws it properly. */
+QJS_AOT_STUB int qjs_aot_array_push_slow(JSContext *ctx, JSValue arr, JSValue v, JSValue *out)
+{
+    JSValue r = js_array_push(ctx, arr, 1, (JSValueConst *)&v, 0);
+
+    if (JS_IsException(r)) {
+        JS_FreeValue(ctx, JS_GetException(ctx));
+        return 0;
+    }
+    *out = r;
+    return 1;
